Subject: [PATCH] netfilter: flowtable: transmit a neigh flow through the route device

Since commit b5964aac51e0 ("netfilter: flowtable: consolidate xmit path"),
a FLOW_OFFLOAD_XMIT_NEIGH entry transmits on the device stored in its
tuple ifidx, and since commit 2bdc536c9da7 ("netfilter: flowtable: always
set route tuple out ifindex") nft_dev_forward_path() takes that device
from dev_fill_forward_path(). Before them the entry transmitted on the
route's device. Two things changed for a route that ends at a bridge:

- When the walk fails, for instance at a mac80211 interface whose driver
  has no .net_fill_forward_path (mt7915 without WED), ifidx stays 0.
  nf_flow_offload_ip_hook() and nf_flow_offload_ipv6_hook() then find no
  output device, tear the flow down and drop the packet. The next packet
  takes the classic path and offloads the flow again, so up to every
  other packet towards a Wi-Fi client is lost.
- When the walk succeeds, ifidx is the bridge port the destination was
  behind when the flow was offloaded. The flow bypasses the bridge: its
  packets skip the bridge netfilter hooks, and keep leaving through that
  port after the forwarding database has moved the address to another.

Default the output device to the route's device, and take it from the
walk only when the path's last device is a flowtable device, as before
those commits. The previous patch keeps such a flow from sending to an
unresolved or departed neighbour, which a bridge would flood to every
port.

Mainline instead refuses to offload a flow whose path cannot be
discovered, in commits 871df5007eda ("netfilter: flowtable: bail out if
forward path cannot be discovered") and 3ae37eafd366 ("netfilter:
flowtable: restore ieee80211 forward path"). Those require the last
device of a bridged path, the bridge port, to be a flowtable device.
The fw4 in OpenWrt 25.12 registers the bridge or its VLAN devices
instead, so with them no bridged LAN flow would be offloaded.
---
 net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c | 5 ++---
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)

--- a/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
+++ b/net/netfilter/nf_flow_table_path.c
@@ -28,6 +28,7 @@ static void nft_default_forward_path(str
 				     enum ip_conntrack_dir dir)
 {
 	route->tuple[!dir].in.ifindex	= dst_cache->dev->ifindex;
+	route->tuple[dir].out.ifindex	= dst_cache->dev->ifindex;
 	route->tuple[dir].dst		= dst_cache;
 	route->tuple[dir].xmit_type	= nft_xmit_type(dst_cache);
 }
@@ -204,12 +205,10 @@ static void nft_dev_forward_path(struct
 	if (nft_dev_fill_forward_path(route, dst, ct, dir, ha, &stack) >= 0)
 		nft_dev_path_info(&stack, &info, ha, &ft->data);

-	if (info.outdev)
-		route->tuple[dir].out.ifindex = info.outdev->ifindex;
-
 	if (!info.indev || !nft_flowtable_find_dev(info.indev, ft))
 		return;

+	route->tuple[dir].out.ifindex = info.outdev->ifindex;
 	route->tuple[!dir].in.ifindex = info.indev->ifindex;
 	for (i = 0; i < info.num_encaps; i++) {
 		route->tuple[!dir].in.encap[i].id = info.encap[i].id;
